# Sample Ooda CLI Spawn Invocations

File: ooda/examples/spawn.oot

Spawn requires `OODACODEX`. The bin is `$OODACODEX/bin/<name>` only. There is no `$PATH` lookup.

## Spawn opm

```sh
ooda opm add foo
ooda opm audit
ooda opm launch --exec foo
```

These spawn `$OODACODEX/bin/opm`. The ooda binary does not link the opm package.

## Spawn lsp

```sh
ooda lsp              # stdio mode (the editor case)
ooda lsp request.txt  # one-shot file mode
```

These spawn `$OODACODEX/bin/lsp`. Stdio is inherited from the ooda process.

## Spawn mcp

```sh
ooda mcp                       # stdio mode
ooda mcp --file request.txt    # one-shot file mode
```

These spawn `$OODACODEX/bin/mcp`.
